From 115431904e900a450308e28ebeaeab4b119bcd52 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Matt Levine <blahm1d@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 5 Jul 2026 09:41:32 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 05/12] core: P0008 - SUBI/CMPI immediates are
 one's-complemented

The TMS34010 stores the ONE'S COMPLEMENT of the operand for the subtracting-
immediate forms SUBI and CMPI, in both the IW (16-bit) and IL (32-bit) forms:
"CMPI 505h" encodes 0xFAFA, "SUBI 4h" encodes 0xFFFB, "CMPI 10EB4E0h" encodes
0xFEF14B1F. The ALU does a - b, so the core must feed ~imm32 to compare/subtract
against the true value. Same encoding-quirk family as P0003 (ANDI); ADDI/ORI/
XORI/MOVI store the immediate as-is.

Fix: split SUBI_IW/CMPI_IW/SUBI_IL/CMPI_IL out of the shared imm32 arm of the
alu_b mux and feed ~imm32.

Surfaced by Smash T.V.'s custom-chip self-test (FFF4E570): the VRAM-palette
readback does CMPI 505h,A3 with A3=0x0505; pre-fix the core compared against
sign-extended 0xFFFFFAFA -> Z=0 -> wrong branch -> "CUSTOM CHIP U99 BAD". Post-fix
the whole test returns A0=0 (PASS), matching MAME. Verified across the entire ROM
via unidasm and vs MAME golden.

