+---
+
+## P0008 — SUBI/CMPI immediate is one's-complemented (CORRECTNESS: every SUBI/CMPI was wrong)
+
+**Status:** ✅ APPLIED + VERIFIED 2026-07-05. `grep -rn P0008 rtl/`.
+
+**Applied edit:** `rtl/core/tms34010_core.sv` (`alu_b` mux) — split the
+subtracting-immediate forms out of the shared `imm32` arm and feed the ALU the
+complement:
+```
+INSTR_SUBI_IW, INSTR_CMPI_IW,
+INSTR_SUBI_IL, INSTR_CMPI_IL: alu_b = ~imm32;   // one's-complement stored imm
+INSTR_MOVI_IW, INSTR_MOVI_IL, INSTR_ADDI_IW, INSTR_ADDI_IL,
+INSTR_ANDI_IL, INSTR_ORI_IL, INSTR_XORI_IL:     alu_b = imm32;   // stored as-is
+```
+
+**Problem.** On the TMS34010 the **subtracting** immediate instructions — `SUBI`
+and `CMPI`, in **both** the IW (16-bit) and IL (32-bit) forms — store the **one's
+complement** of the operand in the immediate field (the ALU forms `a - b` by
+adding the complement + carry). The TI assembler emits `~K`. birdybro's decoder
+fed the raw immediate to `ALU_OP_SUB`/`ALU_OP_CMP`, so `SUBI K` computed
+`Rd - ~K` and `CMPI K` compared against `~K` — **every SUBI/CMPI in every game was
+silently wrong.** (`ADDI`/`ORI`/`XORI`/`MOVI` store the immediate *directly* and
+were already correct; `ANDI`'s complement is handled by `ALU_OP_ANDN`, P0003. This
+is the exact same encoding-quirk family as P0003.)
+
+**Evidence (real ROM + MAME, authoritative).** Verified across the *whole* program
+ROM with `unidasm -arch tms34010` that the immediate word is the one's complement:
+- `CMPI 505h` encodes `0b43 fafa` (`~0x0505 = 0xFAFA`); `CMPI 3h` = `0b40 fffc`;
+  `CMPI 10EB4E0h` (IL) = `0b69 4b1f fef1` (`~0xFEF14B1F`).
+- `SUBI 4h` encodes `0be0 fffb` (`~0x0004 = 0xFFFB`); `SUBI FFE7FD6Dh` (IL) =
+  `0d00 0292 0018` (`~0x00180292`).
+- `ADDI 90h` = `0b0e 0090`, `ORI Ah` = `0ba0 000a 0000`, `XORI 1h` = `0bc0 0001` —
+  all **as-is** (control group; these must NOT complement).
+- **The failure that surfaced it:** the custom-chip self-test (`FFF4E570`) reads
+  back the blitted VRAM palette plane and does `CMPI 505h,A3` with A3=`0x0505`.
+  Pre-fix the core compared `0x0505` against sign-extended `0xFFFFFAFA` → **Z=0**
+  (measured: at `fff4eab0` JRNE, A3=`0x0505` but Z=`0`), so `JRNE` took the fail
+  path → `CUSTOM CHIP U99 BAD`. Post-fix `~imm32 = 0x00000505`, Z=1, the compare
+  passes, and the whole custom-chip test returns A0=0 (PASS), matching MAME
+  (`sim/tb_yunit_custchip.sv`: cmp1 448/448, cmp2 224/224).
+
+**Why boot appeared to "work" before:** like P0003, wrong SUBI/CMPI produced wrong
+*data*/flags, not illegal opcodes, so PC rarely derailed outright — the boot even
+reached the custom-chip test with all setup values matching MAME (the SUBIs on that
+path didn't gate control flow), and only the explicit `CMPI`-against-a-known-constant
+in the self-test exposed it.
+
+**Upstream note.** Real core bug, not Y-unit-specific — offer upstream to birdybro
+together with corrected SUBI/CMPI unit vectors (birdybro's per-instruction TBs pass
+the *un-complemented* immediate, the same blind spot that hid P0003's ANDI).
diff --git a/rtl/core/tms34010_core.sv b/rtl/core/tms34010_core.sv
index dde662b..4e14a48 100644
--- a/rtl/core/tms34010_core.sv
+++ b/rtl/core/tms34010_core.sv
@@ -1913,14 +1913,22 @@ module tms34010_core
   end
   always_comb begin
     unique case (decoded.iclass)
+      // P0008: TMS34010 stores the ONE'S COMPLEMENT of the immediate for the
+      // subtracting-immediate forms SUBI and CMPI (both IW and IL): "CMPI 505h"
+      // encodes 0xFAFA, "SUBI 4h" encodes 0xFFFB, "CMPI 10EB4E0h" encodes
+      // 0xFEF14B1F. The ALU computes a - b, so feed ~imm32 to subtract/compare
+      // against the true value. ADDI/ORI/XORI/MOVI store the immediate as-is;
+      // ANDI's complement is handled separately by ALU_OP_ANDN (P0003). Verified
+      // against MAME/unidasm across the whole ROM; the custom-chip self-test's
+      // `CMPI 505h` was yielding Z=0 for A3=0x505 (blit readback). See PATCHES.md.
+      INSTR_SUBI_IW,
+      INSTR_CMPI_IW,
+      INSTR_SUBI_IL,
+      INSTR_CMPI_IL: alu_b = ~imm32;
       INSTR_MOVI_IW,
       INSTR_MOVI_IL,
       INSTR_ADDI_IW,
-      INSTR_SUBI_IW,
-      INSTR_CMPI_IW,
       INSTR_ADDI_IL,
-      INSTR_SUBI_IL,
-      INSTR_CMPI_IL,
       INSTR_ANDI_IL,
       INSTR_ORI_IL,
       INSTR_XORI_IL: alu_b = imm32;
